==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang}} ''[[discipul]]'', from {{etyl|la}} ''[[discipulus]]'' ‘pupil’; later influenced or superceded in Middle English by {{etyl|fro}} ''[[deciple]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/dɪˈsaɪpəl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who learns from another, especially one who then teaches others.
# An active [[follower]] or [[adherent]] of someone, or some [[philosophy]] etc.

====Translations====
* French: disciple (1,2)

===See also===
* [[apostle]]
* [[discipleship]]

